meta {
  name: List documents
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student-documents?student_id={{studentId}}&verification_status=verified
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.count: eq 1
  res.body.student_documents[0].verification_status: eq verified
  res.body.student_documents[0].document_type: eq birth_certificate
  res.body.page.limit: eq 50
  res.body.page.has_more: eq false
}

docs {
  The sharpest scoping in the collection. Birth certificates, transfer
  certificates and medical papers are the most personal rows the system holds,
  so documents are not gated like the rest of a pupil's record: they sit
  behind the guardian academic gate.

  Concretely, every other guardian-visible thing asks only "is this guardian
  linked to this pupil, and is the link active". Documents add a third
  condition, can_view_academic on that link. A separated parent with contact
  rights but no academic rights reads the home address at 07/07 and gets
  nothing at all here -- same pupil, same active link, different answer. That
  one flag on student_guardians is the whole difference, which makes it worth
  checking before anyone assumes a link is a link.

  Reaching a specific document the caller is not entitled to is 404, not 403.
  Confirming that a birth certificate exists is already a disclosure.
}
